{{also|Verlassen}}

==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/fərˈlasən/|/fɛr-/|[fɐˈlasn̩]|[fɛɐ̯-]|[-sən]}}
* {{hyphenation|de|ver|las|sen}}
* {{audio|de|De-verlassen.ogg|audio}}
* {{audio|de|De-verlassen2.ogg|audio}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|goh|firlāzzan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*fralētaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|verlaten}}, archaic and/or dialectal {{cog|en|forlet}}, and {{cog|gml|vorlaten}}. Equivalent to {{prefix|de|ver|lassen|t1=for-|t2=let, leave}}.

====Verb====
{{de-verb|verlassen<verlässt#verließ,verlassen>}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[leave]], to [[abandon]]; to [[depart]], to [[forsake]]
#: {{ux|de|Die Ratten '''verlassen''' das sinkende Schiff.|The rats are abandoning the sinking ship.}}
#: {{ux|de|Er '''verließ''' das Haus um 7 Uhr.|He left the house at 7 o'clock.}}
## to [[leave]], to [[desert]], to [[dump]] {{gloss|e.g. a partner in a romantic relationship}}
##: {{ux|de|Nach dreijähriger Beziehung '''verließ''' sie ihn.|After three years of an affectionate relationship, she left him.}}
## {{lb|de|figuratively}} to [[pass away]]; to [[cease]]; to [[die]] {{qualifier|with direct object {{m|de|uns}}}}
##: {{ux|de|Es tut mir leid, aber deine Mutter '''hat''' uns gestern Nacht '''verlassen'''.|I am sorry, but your mother passed away last night.}}
## {{lb|de|rare}} to [[exit]] or [[close]] a [[computer program]] or [[app]]
##: {{syn|de|schließen}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive|with {{m|de|auf}} + accusative}} to [[trust]]; to [[rely on]] 
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''verlasse mich''' dar'''auf''', dass du morgen da bist.|I rely on your being there tomorrow.}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''habe''' mich auf dich '''verlassen'''!|I've put my trust in you!}}

